Z||000008||loafer87gt||03-16-2000||07:53 PM||||I got a reply back from Erich on the 89 Replica, here it is guys<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/SouthBeach/Sands/4049/leopard.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/SouthBeach/Sands/4049/leopard.jpg</A> <BR> <BR>  The kit was actually the real body panels from the factory that my Dad had conviced Pontiac not to trash.<BR> <BR>  That's the link to the pic on my site.  When I revamped my Fiero page I didn't feel like putting up a link to it.  Maybe I'll put it back up.  I also have to put up links to the pics of the Arctic Fiero...  It is a Fiero that looks just like my Fiero but with black and white...  Very cool.<BR> <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||william_thorniii||03-16-2000||08:21 PM||||loafer,<P>I find the story VERY difficult to swallow.  It is definitely not like GM to let a prototype out.  Either way, if he has access to the original or some knock off, that could be the easiest way to create an 89 Fiero kit.  Do you think that Eric kid would let us make molds?  <P>Guys, here is the first potential opportunity to get an 89 Fiero.  Personally, I don't care for them, but I know that they are very popular amongst Fiero followers.  <P>Earne,<P>Those triangle lights stumped me for the longest time.  I think I do have a substitute.  Would the triangle lights on the new Cavaliers work out.  They look to be the same to me (from memory).  What do you all think?<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
