Z||000022||DaRkLoRD||03-17-2000||05:09 PM||||Just for fun, last night I created my own "doctored" 89 prototype. I spent 20 minutes on it, and sent the image to a friend of mine. (he's not into cars really) and he didn't notice anything strange. he asked who's car it was. nevermind the bizarre wheelbase gap (the 89 prototype had a longer wheelbase as far as I can tell) and the fact that the body of the car was clearer than the photo it was pasted over (screen grab from a video camera)<P>it'd look more authentic if the image was smaller.. but like I said, it was a 20 minute rush job. I was talking with 2 different people on icq at the same time as I was working as well.<P>sorry for the crappy image edit.. it's just something I threw together.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.lope.net/duckboy/my89fiero.jpg">  <P>btw I put it on a friend's server, as I didn't want this hacked monstrosity on my site.. LOL..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>p.s. most of the 20 minutes was spent cutting out the 89 prototype and erasing the sidescoop and fuel door. then I was looking for a suitable fiero pic to paste it into, and once I found one I spent less than 5 minutes adding the 89 to it.. as is obvious.. horrible editing job. heh.<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 03-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||DaRkLoRD||03-17-2000||05:17 PM||||I might add.. the background photo used to be of a maroon GT with the decklid up.<P>it was the only side shot of a fiero that I could find on short notice. all my other fiero side shot photos aren't the correct perspective.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
